,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.624079134,"data":"--- summary: DDA workload actually timed ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.624756792,"data":"  A throughput number means nothing without the workload behind it. These are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.625552545,"data":"  the mean DDA steps per pixel the timed render kernel executed, measured on\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.62629133,"data":"  the device by replaying the vendored DDA over the same voxels and basis.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.626978978,"data":"entry                          mean DDA steps/pixel       pixels\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.627666739,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.628430651,"data":"  headline_w16 is the number to use. degenerate_w16_ground8 is the SAME shape\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.629118139,"data":"  with ground=8, the configuration the previous run measured; the agent's eye\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.629818956,"data":"  was three blocks inside its own surface, every ray hit on its first voxel\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.630567536,"data":"  test, and the render kernel degenerated into an obs store. It is in this\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.631307411,"data":"  run so the before/after is measured on the same card, not quoted.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.632013065,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.632706528,"data":"Budget: 77/1500 s used.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.633525879,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.634478549,"data":"READING THIS OUTPUT\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.635253065,"data":"  * The three selftest_* entries gate everything. If any says FAIL, the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.63603492,"data":"    numbers below it are not trustworthy and the harness is the suspect.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.636727511,"data":"  * Each entry also gates on a DDA step count. An entry that reports a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.637482013,"data":"    throughput but a mean of ~1.000 steps/pixel is NOT a voxel-render\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.638292283,"data":"    measurement: the render exited on its first voxel test every pixel.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.639108897,"data":"    bench.cu refuses to report timings for such a config unless\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.63971369,"data":"    --measure-degenerate is passed, which is used exactly once here, for the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.640453815,"data":"    entry that exists to document the pre-fix baseline.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.641157169,"data":"  * env-steps/s is batch / median_us. A whole-step number, not a per-kernel one.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.641773295,"data":"  * The measured memory floors in each log are the denominators. %-of-floor\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.642498752,"data":"    figures only mean something against a floor measured on the same card.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.643221098,"data":"  * The author's 49.6M is an RTX 3090 claim. This is a T4. They are not\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":95.643876821,"data":"    comparable numbers and must not be differenced directly.\n"}
